 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479320 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following lines is parallel to $7x + 3y = 6$?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1acd3353-d9a0-58a5-9f78-a462621eb702" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479320 #edb/ref 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $7x + 3y = 6$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 3y &= 6 \\\\\n3y &= -7x + 6 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{7}{3}x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\frac{7}{3}$.\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $-\\frac{7}{3}$ is\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{7}{3}x + \\frac{2}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479342 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479333 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following lines is parallel to $-6x + 5y = 3$?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d211f1c-3b4f-58a0-a29a-a794534e3c55" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479333 #edb/ref 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $-6x + 5y = 3$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x + 5y &= 3 \\\\\n5y &= 6x + 3 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{6}{5}x + \\frac{3}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\frac{6}{5}$.\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $\\frac{6}{5}$ is\n\n$$\ny = \\frac{6}{5}x + \\frac{1}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479322 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479334 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following lines is parallel to $9x - 4y = 11$?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186